// Title: Computer System Reconnaissance Via Wmic.EXE
// Sigma ID: 9d7ca793-f6bd-471c-8d0f-11e68b2f0d2f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-08 | Modified: 2023-02-14
// ATT&CK: discovery, execution, T1047
// Description: Detects execution of wmic utility with the "computersystem" flag in order to obtain information
//   about the machine such as the domain, username, model, etc.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/09/07/profiling-dev-0270-phosphorus-ransomware-operations/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wmic_recon_computersystem.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\wmic.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wmic.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "computersystem"
